WEBVTT

00:06.410 --> 00:08.610
Good morning!  I'm Teika.

00:11.690 --> 00:14.910
In the previous episode,
we introduced these two,

00:14.910 --> 00:17.410
Fujiwara no Michitaka and Takako.

00:15.010 --> 00:17.410
Heian
News

00:15.010 --> 00:17.410
Fujiwara no Michitaka / Takako Get Married!!

00:15.010 --> 00:17.410
Sudden Announcement -
First Child is Born

00:17.850 --> 00:20.300
They were happily married,

00:20.300 --> 00:22.370
and now their first
daughter is over here!

00:22.390 --> 00:29.520
Teishi Enters the Imperial Court!!!

00:22.810 --> 00:25.730
Teishi became the Empress
Consort of Emperor Ichijo.

00:25.730 --> 00:29.310
Michitaka made sure to find a
capable servant for Teishi.

00:29.310 --> 00:33.550
That was Sei Shonagon,
famous for The Pillow Book.

00:33.550 --> 00:39.630
Her family, the Kiyoharas,
was a family of expert poets.

02:11.240 --> 02:14.970
If ever I am unfaithful to you,

02:15.480 --> 02:18.590
the ocean waves will have
reached Mount Suenomatsu.

02:21.940 --> 02:24.980
The waves will never
reach Mount Suenomatsu,

02:25.550 --> 02:28.700
which means that I will
always be faithful to you.

02:30.810 --> 02:34.770
This old poem is why my brother called you,

02:34.770 --> 02:37.420
his first love, Mount Suenomatsu.

02:53.980 --> 02:55.180
Brother?

02:56.320 --> 02:57.920
Is something the matter?

02:59.050 --> 03:00.610
Brother Munenobu?

03:01.560 --> 03:04.270
Nagiko, Mount Suenomatsu has...

03:04.640 --> 03:07.560
No, it wouldn't be right
to call her that now...

03:08.160 --> 03:11.530
It appears that she has wed another man.

03:13.480 --> 03:17.230
This story is set when
I was a young girl,

03:17.230 --> 03:18.710
before I became Sei Shonagon.

03:18.710 --> 03:21.720
Mount Suenomatsu

03:18.710 --> 03:21.720
Kiyohara no Motosuke

03:22.670 --> 03:26.270
Two years ago, our father,
Kiyohara no Motosuke,

03:26.270 --> 03:28.320
completed his service as governor of Suo,

03:28.320 --> 03:31.950
and our family was preparing
to move back to the capital.

03:33.670 --> 03:34.980
Brother?

03:35.600 --> 03:37.920
Honestly, where did he run off to when he's

03:37.920 --> 03:39.360
supposed to be preparing for the move?

03:39.810 --> 03:41.150
Munenobu-sama...

03:41.650 --> 03:43.910
It will be fine, Mount Suenomatsu.

03:44.600 --> 03:46.600
My father said that I must go
through the ceremony of manhood

03:46.600 --> 03:48.470
once we return to the capital.

03:48.470 --> 03:50.560
After that, I will come for you.

03:51.230 --> 03:52.570
Truly?

03:52.570 --> 03:54.450
If you meet a lovely
woman in the capital,

03:54.450 --> 03:55.960
you won't fall for her instead?

03:55.960 --> 03:57.510
I won't.

03:57.510 --> 03:59.460
I swear on your name

03:59.460 --> 04:02.220
that you will be the
only person I ever love.

04:07.370 --> 04:08.590
What?

04:08.590 --> 04:11.990
Munenobu was with a girl
instead of helping?

04:11.990 --> 04:14.790
You should say something, Father!

04:14.790 --> 04:18.070
Nagiko, it would be
improper to interfere

04:18.070 --> 04:19.730
with one of their rare meetings.

04:19.730 --> 04:21.330
You should be more forgiving.

04:22.800 --> 04:26.060
Father, you believe that their
relationship will continue?

04:26.570 --> 04:28.820
My brother said that he would
bring her to the capital

04:28.820 --> 04:30.620
once he went through the
ceremony of manhood.

04:31.910 --> 04:33.250
That will be difficult.

04:33.950 --> 04:36.170
Her family has no rank to speak of,

04:36.170 --> 04:37.900
but they are wealthy.

04:37.900 --> 04:40.650
I doubt they will wed their daughter to

04:40.650 --> 04:41.890
the son of a family on the decline.

04:41.890 --> 04:42.920
On the decline?

04:43.320 --> 04:45.650
You and your self-deprecation...

04:46.110 --> 04:47.210
Nevertheless...

04:49.590 --> 04:53.950
If ever I am unfaithful to you,

04:53.950 --> 04:56.870
the ocean waves will have
reached Mount Suenomatsu.

04:58.130 --> 05:00.400
If they continue to
care for one another,

05:00.400 --> 05:02.950
as in the poem they swore upon,

05:02.950 --> 05:05.970
they will find a way.

05:07.790 --> 05:10.090
I don't like that poem.

05:10.090 --> 05:10.620
Hmm?

05:11.050 --> 05:14.400
Nobody can know what will
happen in the future.

05:14.920 --> 05:19.040
I would never believe such a
promise or make such a promise.

05:19.530 --> 05:20.460
Nagiko...

05:20.950 --> 05:25.100
You shouldn't be so negative.

05:26.880 --> 05:29.890
True.  Regardless of how
strong their feelings are,

05:29.890 --> 05:32.260
the human heart is ever-changing.

05:32.830 --> 05:35.550
If you don't want to be hurt by
a loved one's change of heart,

05:35.550 --> 05:38.980
it would be wise to be skeptical.

05:39.380 --> 05:41.600
But, while there will be no pain,

05:41.600 --> 05:43.440
there will be no joy, either.

05:44.960 --> 05:46.670
Whether it's a promise
or something else,

05:46.670 --> 05:50.710
people truly come alive when they

05:50.710 --> 05:54.270
can believe in something absolute.

05:54.270 --> 05:56.120
That's how they find happiness.

05:57.110 --> 05:59.120
Never forget that, Nagiko.

06:00.010 --> 06:03.500
A life without trust would
be the same as death.

06:08.760 --> 06:10.720
I appreciate all of your help.

06:10.720 --> 06:12.610
Please send a letter once
you reach the capital.

06:12.610 --> 06:14.180
It will be lonely without you.

06:15.310 --> 06:16.730
We're ready to start off,

06:17.080 --> 06:17.960
Munenobu.

06:18.760 --> 06:19.480
Yes.

06:20.020 --> 06:21.600
Munenobu-sama!

06:22.230 --> 06:24.030
Munenobu-sama!

06:24.030 --> 06:25.340
Mount Suenomatsu!

06:25.340 --> 06:28.150
I'll wait for you!

06:28.660 --> 06:30.740
I'll always be waiting for you!

06:32.040 --> 06:33.160
Promise!

06:34.260 --> 06:37.270
Promise that you'll come for me!

06:39.080 --> 06:41.580
Two Years Later, Capital

06:42.930 --> 06:44.130
I see...

06:44.130 --> 06:46.420
Mount Suenomatsu has married.

06:46.900 --> 06:50.060
Munenobu, have you written a reply yet?

06:51.540 --> 06:52.560
No...

06:53.750 --> 06:57.450
I believe it would be disgraceful
to say anything now.

06:58.180 --> 06:59.890
Don't worry.

06:59.890 --> 07:02.850
Since she broke her promise,

07:02.850 --> 07:04.850
you have the right to question her.

07:05.860 --> 07:07.480
Now write a letter.

07:11.220 --> 07:13.450
You haven't the mind to write a poem?

07:14.660 --> 07:16.830
Then I will.

07:18.280 --> 07:21.930
Father, I certainly feel bitter,

07:21.930 --> 07:24.900
but I was also to blame.

07:25.670 --> 07:28.050
I ignored her for two years,

07:28.050 --> 07:30.260
assuming that she would wait.

07:31.760 --> 07:33.950
She was left alone to wait for a man

07:33.950 --> 07:36.090
who might never come.

07:36.960 --> 07:40.850
She must have been subject to
harsh criticism, and felt very lonely.

07:42.750 --> 07:44.430
When I consider her situation,

07:44.430 --> 07:45.900
I can't bring myself to blame her.

07:45.900 --> 07:47.970
In that case,

07:47.970 --> 07:50.270
you need to send a letter of reprimand.

07:50.830 --> 07:52.610
If you show no reaction,

07:52.610 --> 07:56.550
she'll believe that she
was tricked by a bad man.

07:57.950 --> 08:02.530
Though your relationship is
over, your love was true, yes?

08:03.220 --> 08:06.890
There's no reason to ruin that.

08:11.740 --> 08:14.570
You spent the past two years loving her.

08:15.000 --> 08:16.310
You were very loyal.

08:20.640 --> 08:24.240
"A life without trust would
be the same as death."

08:24.780 --> 08:28.930
But it's difficult to
trust someone forever,

08:28.930 --> 08:31.100
care about someone forever.

08:32.820 --> 08:37.430
Will I find something I can believe in?

08:39.290 --> 08:43.650
Impassioned vows exchanged
over many a tear shed

08:43.650 --> 08:47.030
to last until the day waves
crash over Mount Suenomatsu.

08:48.990 --> 08:52.530
They were in tears when they promised

08:52.530 --> 08:54.820
that their love would be forever.

08:56.680 --> 08:58.680
So why...

09:16.320 --> 09:18.790
Hello, again.  Teika here.

09:18.790 --> 09:21.540
When talking about the biggest
studs of the Heian period...

09:21.560 --> 09:30.040
Ariwara no Narihira has found new love!!

09:21.560 --> 09:30.040
Who is
the lucky
girl?!

09:22.250 --> 09:25.440
Ariwara no Narihira would be
the man of the early period.

09:25.440 --> 09:27.450
He's said to have been the
model for Hikaru Genji,

09:27.450 --> 09:30.040
the main character of the Tale of Genji.

09:30.360 --> 09:31.900
If Narihira was the man
of the early period,

09:31.900 --> 09:33.170
the man of the later period
would be this person.

09:33.190 --> 09:40.530
Bamboo Prince Model for Hikaru Genji

09:33.190 --> 09:40.530
Surrounded
by Romantic
Rumors

09:34.090 --> 09:35.930
Fujiwara no Sanekata.

09:35.930 --> 09:38.570
He was also said to have been
the model for Hikaru Genji,

09:38.570 --> 09:40.080
and his elegant manner

09:40.080 --> 09:42.720
was popular with the
ladies of the palace.

09:40.530 --> 09:42.720
Bamboo Prince Frenzy

09:40.530 --> 09:42.720
Sa   ne   ka   ta

09:42.720 --> 09:47.670
Heian News

09:43.160 --> 09:47.180
He was also an excellent poet.

09:57.750 --> 09:59.320
Plum blossoms...

10:01.950 --> 10:04.290
Ah, now there's a face
I haven't seen lately.

10:06.590 --> 10:10.370
Have you forgotten me, Sanekata-sama?

10:11.840 --> 10:14.250
It's been a long time, Nagiko.

10:14.250 --> 10:17.260
Sanekata and Nagiko

10:14.250 --> 10:17.260
The Honorable Fujiwara no Sanekata

10:17.890 --> 10:20.410
I'm worried about my
daughter after her divorce.

10:20.410 --> 10:22.940
Could you look in on
her from time to time?

10:23.880 --> 10:25.900
I received the letter from

10:25.900 --> 10:28.080
Kiyohara no Motosuke-dono five years ago.

10:28.600 --> 10:30.130
"You can have my daughter."

10:30.130 --> 10:32.450
I assumed that was the
underlying message,

10:32.450 --> 10:35.660
so I began to visit Nagiko.

10:37.440 --> 10:40.050
The camellias are in full bloom.

10:40.640 --> 10:43.010
I would love to gaze upon this
winter scenery with you.

10:43.010 --> 10:44.180
Could you raise the curtain

10:44.180 --> 10:46.500
and let me see you, my lady?

10:46.500 --> 10:50.210
Ah, n-no...

10:50.210 --> 10:52.650
I would be embarrassed to ruin

10:52.650 --> 10:56.230
the beautiful flowers with my homely looks.

10:56.230 --> 10:59.130
My lady, your voice is rather distant.

11:00.660 --> 11:02.390
F-Forgive me...

11:03.340 --> 11:05.960
I heard that the divorce was because

11:05.960 --> 11:08.250
she was upset after her
husband was unfaithful.

11:09.650 --> 11:12.350
Women tend to be shy because of

11:12.350 --> 11:15.550
how they're sheltered from a young age.

11:17.290 --> 11:19.230
She probably has the same issue.

11:20.180 --> 11:21.250
Say...

11:21.250 --> 11:22.460
Y-Yes?

11:22.460 --> 11:25.630
It's cold out here, so could
you let me inside the curtain?

11:25.630 --> 11:26.370
Huh?

11:26.370 --> 11:30.120
I came all the way through
the cold to see you.

11:31.040 --> 11:34.820
Can you accept my true feelings?

11:36.060 --> 11:39.540
If you aren't going to
respond, I'll let myself in.

11:39.540 --> 11:41.200
P-Please wait.

11:41.200 --> 11:43.470
I'm going to summon my servant.

11:43.470 --> 11:45.600
Your voice is too distant.

11:46.230 --> 11:48.480
I must come closer to hear what you say.

11:50.340 --> 11:51.880
P-Please wait!

11:51.880 --> 11:53.470
It's too early!

11:53.470 --> 11:55.880
W-We should go through
all the steps first!

11:55.880 --> 11:57.190
Steps?

11:57.650 --> 12:00.640
F-First, w-we exchange poems

12:00.640 --> 12:03.530
to determine if our
feelings are sincere...

12:03.990 --> 12:06.760
I'm not very confident about my poetry.

12:08.490 --> 12:12.540
When I must hide these burning feelings,

12:13.250 --> 12:16.710
I feel as though my body is
on fire with Ibuki mugwort.

12:19.950 --> 12:23.570
I am unable to express my love in words.

12:24.180 --> 12:25.630
That is why I wish to touch you,

12:25.630 --> 12:28.020
so you can feel my burning passion.

12:30.110 --> 12:31.620
Y-Yes...

12:33.860 --> 12:35.140
She's so innocent.

12:35.760 --> 12:38.550
I can't wait to see how she changes.

12:40.800 --> 12:42.780
You said you would be
coming this evening!

12:43.700 --> 12:46.140
I was about to give up and go to bed.

12:46.140 --> 12:47.410
Forgive me.

12:47.410 --> 12:50.880
I search for your flower,
only to be entranced

12:50.880 --> 12:52.620
by its beauty.

12:53.670 --> 12:56.250
I was late because I was looking
for a flower that would suit you.

12:56.660 --> 12:58.140
You're lying!

12:58.140 --> 13:02.120
When drink begins to flow
freely, spring is in the air.

13:02.120 --> 13:04.720
I don't want to hear excuses,
when you went out drinking.

13:05.550 --> 13:07.430
I despise drunkards.

13:08.960 --> 13:10.320
That was a mistake.

13:10.320 --> 13:13.180
I didn't realize that you
knew the rest of the poem.

13:13.180 --> 13:13.840
Oh?

13:13.840 --> 13:16.720
Bai Juyi is basic reading.

13:16.720 --> 13:20.060
Perhaps, but most women wouldn't

13:20.060 --> 13:22.340
reveal their knowledge of Chinese poetry.

13:22.340 --> 13:26.070
Especially not when
trying to outwit a man.

13:27.720 --> 13:30.080
Um, did I upset you?

13:30.080 --> 13:30.960
Hmm?

13:31.610 --> 13:35.540
I know that I shouldn't be like this.

13:36.030 --> 13:39.070
I have a habit of showing off my
knowledge instead of being supportive.

13:40.010 --> 13:40.920
I'll try to be more careful,

13:41.470 --> 13:43.300
so please don't despise me.

13:45.510 --> 13:48.250
Nagiko, I was speaking in general.

13:49.060 --> 13:51.840
Personally, I like that part of you.

13:52.490 --> 13:54.430
That part of me?

13:54.650 --> 13:58.620
I love how you make witty
and cheeky comments.

13:59.480 --> 14:02.120
What?  Are you calling me cheeky?

14:06.280 --> 14:08.840
Sanekata-sama, wake up.

14:10.390 --> 14:11.950
It's already dawn?

14:12.770 --> 14:15.940
I wouldn't mind enjoying this
spring morning by sleeping in.

14:15.940 --> 14:19.120
Please, don't say that.

14:19.620 --> 14:22.650
It would be a waste to sleep
through a spring morning.

14:22.650 --> 14:23.780
Why?

14:23.780 --> 14:26.090
Please look outside.

14:27.130 --> 14:31.470
The wispy clouds hover around
the mountains as the sun rises,

14:31.470 --> 14:33.560
creating a violet sky.

14:34.670 --> 14:37.550
A magical dawn that could
call down the gods.

14:38.310 --> 14:41.980
No dawn is as beautiful as a dawn in spring.

14:44.390 --> 14:45.460
Sanekata-sama?

14:45.460 --> 14:48.250
Yes, let's go back to bed.

14:48.670 --> 14:49.820
You have no discipline.

14:50.220 --> 14:54.400
Nagiko, I doubt there's
another woman like you.

14:54.400 --> 14:56.120
Oh, what's this about?

14:57.350 --> 15:01.230
I'm trembling with joy after
discovering a beautiful spring

15:01.230 --> 15:02.960
in an unexpected place.

15:02.960 --> 15:04.860
I never dreamed

15:04.860 --> 15:09.720
that I would find someone
who truly understood me.

15:10.140 --> 15:14.180
Nagiko, I love your wit.

15:14.820 --> 15:17.960
I will be the person who
understands you best.

15:19.630 --> 15:21.130
Say, Sanekata.

15:21.130 --> 15:23.610
Are you still courting
Motosuke's daughter?

15:23.910 --> 15:26.480
What now, Kinto?

15:26.480 --> 15:28.540
I happened to hear...

15:28.540 --> 15:31.950
that Michitaka-sama
requested that Motosuke's

15:31.950 --> 15:33.790
daughter serve in the palace.

15:35.440 --> 15:38.420
Ah, it must be for Teishi-sama's sake.

15:38.420 --> 15:42.820
Yes, he mentioned before that he wanted

15:42.820 --> 15:44.480
intelligent servants for his daughter.

15:45.100 --> 15:48.420
He's been making inquiries
since the new year began.

15:48.700 --> 15:50.810
If Motosuke's daughter
becomes a servant,

15:50.810 --> 15:52.560
she will be more valuable.

15:52.560 --> 15:55.010
So how is her mind?

15:55.900 --> 15:58.810
Sharp.  She's a smart lady.

15:59.450 --> 16:01.350
You sound confident.

16:01.350 --> 16:02.400
What?

16:02.400 --> 16:05.230
An intelligent woman will
attract much attention here.

16:05.730 --> 16:08.410
What if she enters into the palace,
with all its temptations,

16:08.410 --> 16:11.570
and falls for another man?

16:12.150 --> 16:14.520
I'll work hard to make sure
that doesn't happen.

16:15.050 --> 16:17.020
I would never rob my beloved

16:17.020 --> 16:19.720
of an opportunity because it
was inconvenient for me.

16:20.280 --> 16:22.040
Excuse me, then.

16:22.330 --> 16:26.110
I've heard that Teishi-sama
is a very bright lady.

16:26.110 --> 16:31.010
Nagiko will be able to use her
wit if she serves Teishi-sama.

16:31.950 --> 16:34.590
I understand her better
than anyone else.

16:36.320 --> 16:37.420
What?

16:37.420 --> 16:40.430
You already heard about
the invitation to serve?

16:40.430 --> 16:43.460
Yes, it sounds like you've
been hesitant to respond.

16:43.460 --> 16:44.460
Why is that?

16:44.460 --> 16:46.550
I wanted to talk to you first.

16:47.220 --> 16:50.030
You have an excellent mind.

16:50.330 --> 16:52.410
It would be a good idea to see

16:52.410 --> 16:54.680
the outside world and use your talent.

16:54.680 --> 16:58.150
But a learned woman like myself

16:58.150 --> 16:59.990
will stand out in the palace.

17:01.160 --> 17:04.410
You and my father are the only nobles

17:04.910 --> 17:07.080
who have ever accepted me.

17:07.310 --> 17:09.620
Nagiko, there are many

17:09.620 --> 17:12.920
ladies in the court who
make use of their wits.

17:14.180 --> 17:18.060
You have the potential
to outshine them all.

17:18.060 --> 17:19.300
R-Really?

17:19.300 --> 17:22.520
I'm not educated enough

17:22.520 --> 17:25.290
to appreciate everything you say,

17:25.290 --> 17:26.600
but in the palace,

17:26.600 --> 17:29.280
you'll meet people who do understand.

17:29.280 --> 17:30.850
In that respect, you'll find people

17:30.850 --> 17:34.970
who are truly able to
understand you, perhaps...

17:35.890 --> 17:37.600
I see now...

17:38.950 --> 17:41.350
After Nagiko becomes a servant,
she will drift away from me.

17:41.890 --> 17:43.250
Once she holds a meaningful position

17:43.780 --> 17:45.650
and meets people who understand her,

17:45.650 --> 17:48.180
she will lose interest in me.

17:48.780 --> 17:50.170
That's what I fear.

17:51.330 --> 17:55.410
That shows how I love her talent.

17:56.260 --> 17:57.300
But...

17:57.950 --> 17:59.350
It is beyond me...

18:00.140 --> 18:02.060
I-I think I'll pass.

18:02.060 --> 18:03.060
Huh?

18:03.060 --> 18:05.560
I'm not as smart as you think.

18:06.110 --> 18:08.580
Serving in the palace would
be completely different.

18:08.580 --> 18:13.030
Besides, I'll be fine, as
long as you understand me.

18:13.730 --> 18:15.680
I want to devote myself to one person,

18:15.680 --> 18:18.490
a person who would also
devote himself to me.

18:18.940 --> 18:21.570
That is the life I want to lead.

18:22.500 --> 18:24.700
As long as you're by my
side, I'll be satisfied.

18:24.970 --> 18:28.330
You only say that because you've
been living in a small world.

18:28.330 --> 18:29.340
What?

18:30.110 --> 18:33.210
I chose you out of many,

18:33.210 --> 18:34.920
but it was different in your case.

18:35.590 --> 18:37.940
You let yourself fall
for a man who happened

18:37.940 --> 18:41.330
to be there and somewhat understood you.

18:41.940 --> 18:43.330
Once you've seen the rest of the world,

18:43.330 --> 18:44.640
your feelings will change.

18:44.640 --> 18:45.640
That's not true!

18:45.980 --> 18:49.720
You may think that I've been
living in a small world

18:49.720 --> 18:51.230
and know nothing about what's outside,

18:51.230 --> 18:56.190
but I chose to pursue such a life,
and still set my heart on you!

18:56.630 --> 18:59.150
I truly love you!

19:04.190 --> 19:05.500
Will you come back tonight?

19:06.070 --> 19:10.570
No, I'll be busy with work for
a while, so it'll be difficult.

19:10.950 --> 19:11.630
I see.

19:11.920 --> 19:14.440
I'll send you a letter.  Bye.

19:16.680 --> 19:19.190
Sanekata-sama!  I...

19:20.510 --> 19:23.370
You're all I need...  So...

19:25.520 --> 19:29.460
I believe that your feelings are true.

19:32.030 --> 19:33.430
However, Nagiko...

19:34.120 --> 19:36.020
You haven't seen the ocean yet...

19:37.880 --> 19:40.090
You were meant to sail the seas.

19:43.400 --> 19:45.490
Yes, thank you.

19:48.780 --> 19:50.560
You'll see me soon.

19:51.560 --> 19:52.540
Yes.

20:06.640 --> 20:08.370
I didn't think you

20:08.370 --> 20:12.060
would ignore me for such a long time.

20:12.670 --> 20:14.860
I must have imagined that you said

20:14.860 --> 20:18.390
I would see you soon, Sanekata-sama.

20:18.980 --> 20:23.580
Well, the seasons meant
little to me without you.

20:23.970 --> 20:26.660
I forgot how much time
had passed, Nagiko...

20:26.660 --> 20:28.700
Do not call me by that name.

20:28.700 --> 20:31.250
I am now known as Sei Shonagon.

20:31.780 --> 20:32.980
Shonagon...

20:33.490 --> 20:34.710
How did that happen?

20:35.190 --> 20:37.360
The Empress Consort gave me the title

20:37.360 --> 20:39.170
because it sounded nice.

20:41.200 --> 20:43.260
She must really like you.

20:43.770 --> 20:48.560
Yes, I found something to believe in.

20:49.060 --> 20:51.010
Sounds like you're doing well.

20:51.010 --> 20:52.740
Yes, thanks to you.

20:52.740 --> 20:55.510
Oh, do you hold a grudge?

20:55.510 --> 20:57.190
You were the one who left me.

20:57.660 --> 20:59.860
You believe that I left you?

20:59.860 --> 21:01.530
Oh?  Are you saying that isn't the case?

21:02.910 --> 21:03.990
I wouldn't know.

21:08.180 --> 21:09.330
Sei Shonagon-dono.

21:10.760 --> 21:14.050
You must have found many
people who understand you.

21:14.050 --> 21:15.830
It was I who told you that would happen,

21:16.350 --> 21:19.560
but the people in the palace are
manipulative and opportunistic.

21:20.200 --> 21:23.050
Be careful when you deal with them.

21:23.560 --> 21:25.810
Consider this a warning from a friend.

21:26.640 --> 21:27.520
Thank you.

21:28.170 --> 21:30.010
I'll remember that.

21:33.270 --> 21:35.420
A winter spent in courtship

21:36.150 --> 21:38.020
that led to a brief love
which ended in spring.

21:38.910 --> 21:42.280
The seasons turn and flowers bloom...

21:43.050 --> 21:46.500
Fitting for my reunion with her.

21:48.240 --> 21:54.940
Like a fish in water, she
will gain confidence

21:54.940 --> 21:59.540
and charm as she swims through the ocean.

22:00.040 --> 22:03.320
She will always be beyond me.

22:04.180 --> 22:08.660
So now, I repeat that poem I
composed for you that spring.

22:10.340 --> 22:12.370
When I must hide these burning feelings,

22:12.370 --> 22:18.180
I feel as though my body is
on fire with Ibuki mugwort.

22:19.960 --> 22:23.800
I can never tell you
how much I love you.

22:24.600 --> 22:26.650
That is why you will never know

22:28.480 --> 22:30.710
how I truly feel.

22:32.910 --> 22:34.950
Poetic Tale 8:

22:32.910 --> 22:34.950
END

24:04.960 --> 24:25.000
Next
Episode

24:04.960 --> 24:25.000
Shonagon and Yukinari

24:04.960 --> 24:25.000
Sei Shonagon

24:07.250 --> 24:12.190
Said night was young when
the false rooster crowed,

24:13.110 --> 24:17.280
but the gates of Afusaka remained shut.
